Generally, there are two things here:
(1) yes rainbird can't handle concurrent requests from multiple things and will reject requests when they arrive at the same time. have had to work through instability in the past as a result of this
(2) the rainbird integration has to query a device after sending a command to check its latest state, otherwise it reverts back to old state for a very long time until the next poll.
but i have never seen any of these crash anything.


