looks like this has been fixed, I just tested a few times now. AI says:

PR #172002 — Almost certainly your fix (merged May 24, 2026)
Root cause: The Rain Bird LNK Wi-Fi module can only handle one HTTP request at a time. The HA integration has two background coordinators — RainbirdUpdateCoordinator (polls zone states) and RainbirdScheduleUpdateCoordinator (fetches calendar/schedule) — running on independent timers. When they overlapped, the device sent back NAK (busy) responses.
What that caused:
Zones marked unavailable when the device NAK'd a state poll
When you commanded a zone to run, the schedule coordinator could fire simultaneously — the device getting confused between the concurrent requests is consistent with running for both the default program time and the commanded run time
