Thanks, I will investigate. Have you tried the Cloud API as well? Most climate devices aren't supported in local API.

If I use my cloud box from atlantic, it works but if possible i want to avoid cloud 😁

Thanks for the diagnostics! Over the Local API your ventilation unit doesn't report `io:VentilationModeState`, and the climate entity assumes it's always there. That's why it crashes and floods the log. I'll fix it so the entity loads without that state.

Note that climate devices are currently not (fully) supported via the Local API, see [Device support via the Local API](https://www.home-assistant.io/integrations/overkiz/#device-support-via-the-local-api). This is tracked upstream in Somfy-Developer/Somfy-TaHoma-Developer-Mode#20. Until that's resolved, the Cloud API is the recommended way to control this device.

