@frenck so the config interval in the hive integration doesn’t control how often home assistant calls the pyhive-integration. It actually get passed to the pyhive-integration at startup and what this controls is how often the hive-integration library polls the hive api services. So the default is 2 minutes and using the config option they can reduce this but not below 30 seconds to prevent constant and aggressive load on the hive APIs.

Happy to look at renaming this if needed but the key thing here is it doesn’t control how often home assist t calls the integration library. That’s set to 15 seconds currently and home assistant will get cached data back on its 15 second intervals until the pyhive-integration has refreshed its data on its own schedule driven by this config

> this controls is how often the hive-integration library polls the hive api services

That is exactly what we do not allow to be controlled 😄

@frenck  any particular reason it’s not allowed?

I understand it from a home assistant to integration library point of view. What’s the concern around controlling the polling to external services. Some people may not want the data refreshed as often as 2 minutes which is the default currently.

The concern is that more often the values are changed to numbers that case stability issues (not just on our end). This is not something a user should be concerned about to begin with.

If an power user really wants, there are home assistant services available to trigger updates on any schedule with any condition one wishes (which is more flexible than a setting). For that reason, we do not allow them.

For more information check our developer documentation where this rule is documented.

