This is materially different from #55187. That PR broadly changes merge failures to `ValueError`, but the cache-group compatibility probes currently catch `AssertionError`; changing only the exception type turns an ordinary incompatibility into a startup failure. It also leaves the target/draft marker as an allocation constraint.

