query:
[KV Connector][Offloading] Canonical MLA+DSA secondary transfers use TP-dependent row sizes

`canonical_layout: true` gives certified MLA+DSA configurations a topology-free storage namespace, but secondary transfers still use the full aligned primary-tier row. That row can change size with TP, so compatible canonical payloads fail P2P connection validation or filesystem promotion.

## Recorded reproduction

The 2026-09-09 smoke notes record these results on H200 nodes:

- Image: `vllm/vllm-openai:nightly-385dce36bcee42309924a5ece951a96db3dce7f2`, which includes #51690 (`df09c767355fd1313001fbf14ad363bba5bf0ffd`).
- Model: `zai-org/GLM-5.2-FP8`, truncated to four layers with `--hf-overrides` so TP1 and TP2 fit alongside other workloads. The entrypoint filters absent-layer checkpoint tensors before loading. This is not a full-model validation.
- `OffloadingConnector` with `TieringOffloadingSpec`, `canonical_layout: true`, `offload_prompt_only: false`, `--kv-cache-dtype fp8`, `--block-size 64`, `PYTHONHASHSEED=0`, and `VLLM_USE_V2_MODEL_RUNNER=0`.
- For the shared-namespace FS tests, TP1 uses `--distributed-executor-backend mp`; both engines record `tp_size: 1` and `canonical_format: v1-hnd`.

| Tier | Writer -> reader | External hits | Recorded result |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| P2P | TP1 -> TP2 | 0 / 24147 | `rejecting peer connect: block_len mismatch ... remote=196608, local=389120` |
| FS, shared namespace | TP2 -> TP1 | 24128 / 24147 | 74,121,216 bytes read |
| FS, shared namespace | TP1 -> TP2 | 0 / 24147 | `block I/O failed: [Errno 5] Input/output error` |

These figures come from the recorded smoke notes. The source review below does not constitute an independent GPU rerun. Tier hits establish reuse, not model-output correctness.

## Source trace

Checked at upstream `663d7f679eda78a8d48613dfede8a4b4bcff2b74`; the cited paths are unchanged at `e6b4e47d2d894a1a0815fbf03669adb1b3405083`.

1. [CPUOffloadingSpec](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/663d7f679eda78a8d48613dfede8a4b4bcff2b74/vllm/v1/kv_offload/cpu/spec.py#L109-L127) calculates row bytes as `round_up(worker_kv_bytes_per_block * num_copies * blocks_per_chunk, BLOCK_SIZE_ALIGNMENT)`, where `num_copies = 1 if replicated_layout else world_size`. Canonical layout does not change this allocation formula.
2. [SharedOffloadRegion](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/663d7f679eda78a8d48613dfede8a4b4bcff2b74/vllm/v1/kv_offload/cpu/shared_offload_region.py#L282-L326) packs canonical tensor areas into the row prefix but exposes a memoryview spanning the full row to secondary tiers, including unused trailing bytes.
3. [P2P transport](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/663d7f679eda78a8d48613dfede8a4b4bcff2b74/vllm/v1/kv_offload/tiering/p2p/data/nixl.py#L101-L106) uses row length for both block addressing and transfer length. The [session handshake](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/663d7f679eda78a8d48613dfede8a4b4bcff2b74/vllm/v1/kv_offload/tiering/p2p/session/session.py#L448-L456) rejects unequal lengths before comparing config fingerprints.
4. The [FS manager](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/663d7f679eda78a8d48613dfede8a4b4bcff2b74/vllm/v1/kv_offload/tiering/fs/manager.py#L167) uses `primary_kv_view.strides[0]` as the I/O size. The [native reader](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/663d7f679eda78a8d48613dfede8a4b4bcff2b74/csrc/fs_io.cpp#L82-L105) accepts a prefix read from a larger file, but returns `EIO` and unlinks the source file on a short read. File deletion is a source-derived consequence, not a separately recorded observation from this smoke run.

## Relationship to the canonical-layout PRs

[#51690](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/51690) certifies the individual specs inside `UniformTypeKVCacheSpecs`; its diff changes the static gate and tests. Its reported GPU validation is a same-TP8 FS round trip. It does not change row sizing or secondary transfer descriptors.

Cross-TP support does exist for narrower configurations. [#49858](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/49858) makes secondary identity TP-independent for compact replicated MLA rows, whose width is already TP-independent. That gate excludes wrapped/mixed MLA+DSA groups. This report concerns canonical configurations whose physical row widths differ across TP sizes.

## Expected behavior

Certified canonical peers should exchange the canonical payload for each chunk with a topology-independent transfer length. Source and destination addressing must still use their respective physical row strides, unless allocation itself produces compact canonical rows. Removing or reordering the handshake length check alone does not satisfy that requirement.

## Independent namespace issue affecting the reproduction

With TP1's default `uni` executor, the smoke notes record `dtype: fp8_ds_mla`; TP2 with `mp` records `dtype: fp8`. The [MLA worker](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/663d7f679eda78a8d48613dfede8a4b4bcff2b74/vllm/model_executor/layers/attention/mla_attention.py#L510) mutates `cache_config.cache_dtype`, and [offloading config construction](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/663d7f679eda78a8d48613dfede8a4b4bcff2b74/vllm/distributed/kv_transfer/kv_connector/v1/offloading/config.py#L239-L240) reads that value. `uni` shares the config with the scheduler process. Forcing TP1 to `mp` isolates this namespace split in the recorded FS tests; it does not fix row-size incompatibility.

## Reproduction artifacts

The manifest and gate script below are the files used for the recorded run, with two later edits: the TP1 pod pins `--distributed-executor-backend mp` (see the namespace section), and the gate script now requires a positive read-bytes delta on the tier under test rather than aggregate hits, so an FS read cannot satisfy a P2P check. The logs are the recorded outputs and engine log lines from 2026-09-09; the pods are gone, so no fuller logs exist.

