@Yunzez I looked into this one, The root cause is that get_mamba_state_shape_from_config on the affected models calls mamba2_state_shape without num_spec, while the live MambaMixer2.get_state_shape passes num_spec=self.num_spec — so the planned padded page is sized for conv_kernel-1 columns and the real state is conv_kernel-1+num_spec wide, tripping assert page_size_padded >= page_size in MambaSpec.page_size_bytes.

This is already a solved pattern in-tree: mamba2.py, nemotron_h.py, qwen3_next.py, and olmo_hybrid.py thread num_spec into the calculator. The ones missing it are granitemoehybrid.py, falcon_h1.py, zamba2.py (all mamba2_state_shape), and lfm2.py / lfm2_moe.py (short_conv_state_shape, which also accepts num_spec). jamba.py (mamba1) and bailing_moe_linear.py (linear attn) have no conv-state widening and are unaffected.

Proposed fix: pass num_spec=vllm_config.num_speculative_tokens in those five classmethods, matching the existing convention. Happy to open a PR soon.

@Yunzez upon running duplicate check, I found #47635 already fixes this for GraniteMoeHybrid / FalconH1 / Zamba2 (all mamba2_state_shape callers) and adds a message to the bare assert — that PR is mergeable and just needs a ready label for CI.

One additional instance not covered by #47635: lfm2.py and lfm2_moe.py call short_conv_state_shape (which also accepts num_spec) and omit it. Their ShortConv mixer does support multi-token verify (short_conv.py reads num_accepted_tokens and passes num_spec in get_state_shape), so this is the same defect and the same one-line fix applies — unlike PLaMo2, which #47635 correctly leaves out.

